From 458e0605fa8c10d8f80c73d2862b26ed54473eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Shevlyakov <igor@tachyum.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:32:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] testsuite: Skip pr128080.c at -O0

The permutations in pr128080.c are merged only when optimizing, so at
-O0 the test checks nothing.  It is also slow there on some targets:
on arm-eabi with -march=armv6s-m (Thumb-1) LRA spends more than ten
minutes on the two 256-element shuffles that survive to RTL, and the
compilation times out.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c: Skip at -O0.

Signed-off-by: Igor Shevlyakov <igor@tachyum.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2563111c38bc59ba4a1fc60cbfd714d4bac94b15)
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c
index cb0410c4997c..b84e6c1640ba 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128080.c
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 /* PR tree-optimization/128080 */
 /* { dg-do run } */
+/* The permutations are merged only when optimizing.  */
+/* { dg-skip-if "" { *-*-* } { "-O0" } { "" } } */
 /* { dg-additional-options "-Wno-psabi" } */
 
 typedef signed char V __attribute__((vector_size (256)));
